															</div>
				<div class="info">
					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/cybersqyd" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5336470); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=5336470&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607200906" alt="cybersqyd" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=5336470)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/cybersqyd" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(5336470); return false;" >cybersqyd</a></span> <span class="odate time_1578304900 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">06 Jan 2020 10:01</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-4462230">
									

<p>Hm. I kinda really dig the concept here and there's a lot of imagery and potential; but it kinda feels like this doesn't quite do enough with the idea here? I'm really not sure how I'm expected to feel about this SCP: generally a huge organism living under a city should be bad but it seems kinda benign; and it has some connection with sewage so maybe it's like eating sewage or something and could be good? I don't really feel terrified or disgusted by this or really anything at all.</p>
<p>It kinda feels like it needs more: some kind of stakes or indication of what the consequences of this thing existing are? Possibly some kind of exploration of what's inside it so you can really convey the horror/weirdness of it?</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;minor&nbsp;things</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<blockquote>
<p>Non-Foundational personnel and civilians observing or otherwise interacting with SCP-4594 are to be amnesticised where necessary.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>I'm not generally a fan of vague phrasing like &quot;where necessary&quot; in the ConProcs: like, to me, the ConProcs should have some indication of when it's necessary to amnesticise someone who interacts with the SCP: is it just if they realise it's not regular plumbing? is it just if they're posting about the SCP's existence a lot on social media?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>across, and is limited to, the area of Greater London.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Hm. The phrasing &quot;is limited to&quot; implies &quot;it can't leave Greater London&quot; but it seems like it could if it wanted to, it just doesn't want to?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-4594’s interior is host to an indeterminate number of rodents and other small mammals that use the object as a means of travel.</p>
</blockquote>
<blockquote>
<p>SCP-4594’s occupants are docile and do not actively interact with one another, instead remaining limp while within SCP-4594.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Small mammals using it as a means of travel but remaining limp while within the SCP feels a little weird here? Are you intending to convey that it's kinda like a <a href="https://theinfosphere.org/Tube_Transport_System">futurama style people tube</a> rather than like &quot;the animals run across it&quot;?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>Since 2003, the application of specialized ground-penetrating radar has enabled the Foundation</p>
</blockquote>
<p>It feels kinda weird that for about 30 years, the Foundation knew this existed but didn't use radar to track it? From what I can tell, ground-penetrating radar has existed since 1910 and like, there were developments in it during the 70s which meant it really started to take off then?</p>
<blockquote>
<p>was found lodged between the plumbing in a way</p>
</blockquote>
<p>Something about the phrasing here feels, a little clunky? I think because normally &quot;between&quot; features two things (&quot;between a rock and a hard place&quot;) and here you just have one (the plumbing): perhaps &quot;around&quot; or &quot;within&quot; would work better than between?</p>
<p>&#8230;.Honestly part of me feels like something more evocative should be used here? This is very, dry and factual and it feels like an opportunity to really convey&#8230;something.</p>
</div>
</div>
</div>

